{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "TIT",
  "chapter": 2,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "TIT.2.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.2.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But speak thou the things which become sound doctrine:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.2.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.2.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That the aged men be sober, grave, temperate, sound in faith, in charity, in patience;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.2.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.2.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The aged women likewise, that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "they be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in behavior as becometh holiness, not false accusers, not given to much wine, teachers of good things;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.2.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.2.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That they may teach the young women to be sober, to love their husbands, to love their children,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.2.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.2.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " discreet, chaste, keepers at home, good, obedient to their own husbands, that the word of God be not blasphemed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.2.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.2.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Young men likewise exhort to be sober-minded.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.2.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.2.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In all things showing thyself a pattern of good works: in doctrine ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "showing",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " incorruptness, gravity, sincerity,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.2.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.2.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Sound speech that cannot be condemned; that he that is of the contrary part may be ashamed, having no evil thing to say concerning you.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.2.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.2.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Exhort",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " servants to be obedient to their own masters, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to please ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " well in all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "; not answering again;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.2.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.2.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Not purloining, but showing all good fidelity; that they may adorn the doctrine of God our Savior in all things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.2.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.2.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the grace of God that bringeth salvation hath appeared to all men,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.2.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.2.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Teaching us, that denying ungodliness, and worldly lusts, we should live soberly, righteously, and piously, in this present world;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.2.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.2.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Looking for that blessed hope, and the glorious appearing of the great God, and our Savior Jesus Christ;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.2.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.2.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who gave himself for us, that he might redeem us from all iniquity, and purify to himself a peculiar people, zealous of good works.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "TIT.2.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:TIT.2.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "These things speak, and exhort, and rebuke with all authority. Let no man despise thee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
